NAME
    write - write one byte to a memory space

SYNOPSIS
    write <space> <addr> <value>

DESCRIPTION
    Writes a single hex byte <value> into memory space <space> at hex
    address <addr>. Refuses read-only memory spaces (see spaces(1)).

    For persistent per-frame writes or ROM-read intercepts, use cheat(1).
    For bulk writes from a file, use load(1).

EXAMPLES
    write WRAM 10 ff

EXIT STATUS
    0   Byte written (or usage/read-only refusal printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid hex argument, or
        session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    mem(1), load(1), dump(1), spaces(1), cheat(1)
